  "description": "WUMWOQ crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group P n -3 n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C160 H152 Eu9 O42 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+,2(C1 H4 O1),C1 H1 Cl3. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1K (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1I (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1KA (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1J (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1LA (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1JA (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1UA (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.673-5.194 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.47-168.91°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C169H177Cl3NO44Eu9. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
